WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.880
College

00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:02.200
costs a fortune.

00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:04.820
Most Americans can't afford tuition.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:05.880
Fortunately

00:00:05.880 --> 00:00:06.840
some colleges

00:00:06.840 --> 00:00:08.420
now put their professors lectures

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.360
online

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:09.860
so

00:00:09.860 --> 00:00:11.340
everyone can learn.

00:00:11.340 --> 00:00:12.440
Here's a sample

00:00:12.440 --> 00:00:14.860
How we derive energy

00:00:14.860 --> 00:00:16.420
from triglyceride

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:17.760
This Berkeley video

00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:19.440
makes chemistry interesting.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.560
because carbon and hydrogen are nonpolar

00:00:22.560 --> 00:00:24.020
those are insoluble

00:00:24.020 --> 00:00:25.020
For five years

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.540
anyone could access

00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:28.220
20,000 videos

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.620
on Berkeley's website.

00:00:29.625 --> 00:00:30.324
But then

00:00:30.324 --> 00:00:32.103
President Obama's Justice Department

00:00:32.103 --> 00:00:34.700
sent Berkeley this threatening letter

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:37.280
Berkeley's in violation of title 2

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:39.856
The Attorney General may initiate a lawsuit.

00:00:39.856 --> 00:00:41.994
It's all because of a well intended law

00:00:41.994 --> 00:00:42.614
called

00:00:42.614 --> 00:00:44.752
the Americans with Disabilities Act.

00:00:44.752 --> 00:00:46.770
Both blatant and subtle discrimination

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.029
A young Al Gore

00:00:48.029 --> 00:00:49.300
pushed for that law.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.480
President Bush senior signed it.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:54.200
Both parties applauded.

00:00:54.200 --> 00:00:54.880
Who wouldn't?

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:55.660
Who could object

00:00:55.660 --> 00:00:56.740
to a law that says

00:00:56.740 --> 00:00:58.080
"No individual

00:00:58.081 --> 00:00:59.060
with a disability

00:00:59.060 --> 00:00:59.760
shall be

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:02.058
denied the benefits of services?

00:01:02.058 --> 00:01:03.077
But as usual,

00:01:03.077 --> 00:01:04.556
the good intentions had

00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:06.300
unintended consequences.

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:07.653
All lectures are being deleted

00:01:07.653 --> 00:01:09.412
so now no one can access them.

00:01:09.412 --> 00:01:11.430
Berkeley took its videos down

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:13.608
because closed captioning is expensive.

00:01:13.608 --> 00:01:15.027
It has to be done by a

00:01:15.027 --> 00:01:16.586
person who listens

00:01:16.586 --> 00:01:18.680
and then types out each word.

00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:22.020
Computers can transcribe cheaply

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:23.460
but they're lousy at it.

00:01:23.460 --> 00:01:24.939
When a Harvard video said

00:01:24.959 --> 00:01:25.958
"on our campus",

00:01:25.958 --> 00:01:27.696
it was transcribed as

00:01:27.696 --> 00:01:29.555
"hot Kampen good".

00:01:29.555 --> 00:01:31.153
Our experienced transcriptionists

00:01:31.160 --> 00:01:34.160
will perfectly transcribe your recordings.

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:35.740
Berkeley didn't want to spend millions

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.228
on companies like this,

00:01:37.228 --> 00:01:38.907
so it blocked everyone

00:01:38.907 --> 00:01:40.546
from seeing its lectures.

00:01:40.546 --> 00:01:42.324
Everyone's treated equally.

00:01:42.324 --> 00:01:43.243
Hearing people

00:01:43.243 --> 00:01:45.200
have no advantage over the deaf.

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:45.960
Nobody

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.640
gets to see the videos.

00:01:47.640 --> 00:01:49.380
Government equality police

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.780
doing their work.

00:01:50.797 --> 00:01:51.297
But

00:01:51.297 --> 00:01:52.096
fortunately

00:01:52.100 --> 00:01:53.980
the videos will survive,

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:55.473
thanks to the internet

00:01:55.473 --> 00:01:57.332
and pissed off entrepreneurs

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:58.920
like Jeremy Kaufman.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:00.240
We're gonna keep it available.

00:02:00.240 --> 00:02:01.540
Kaufman downloaded

00:02:01.540 --> 00:02:03.080
all the Berkeley videos before

00:02:03.087 --> 00:02:04.705
they were taken down

00:02:04.705 --> 00:02:05.645
and reposted them

00:02:05.645 --> 00:02:06.960
to his web site

00:02:06.960 --> 00:02:07.740
LBRY,

00:02:07.743 --> 00:02:09.100
spelled funny.

00:02:09.222 --> 00:02:10.461
The Justice Department might say

00:02:10.461 --> 00:02:11.760
you're making life

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:13.138
tougher for deaf people.

00:02:13.298 --> 00:02:14.897
I don't think anyone thinks that

00:02:14.997 --> 00:02:16.016
it wouldn't be better

00:02:16.016 --> 00:02:18.514
if stuff were subtitled for deaf people

00:02:18.514 --> 00:02:19.473
but at the same time

00:02:19.473 --> 00:02:20.812
it's ridiculous to say this content

00:02:20.812 --> 00:02:22.750
can't be available unless

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:24.229
it's subtitled for deaf people.

00:02:24.260 --> 00:02:27.040
Kaufman says he wants to help deaf people

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:28.600
but when closed captioning

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.000
costs millions,

00:02:30.004 --> 00:02:31.523
Is that a reason that content

00:02:31.523 --> 00:02:33.561
shouldn't be available to everyone?

00:02:33.561 --> 00:02:35.180
Do you want to put a gun to someone's face

00:02:35.180 --> 00:02:36.359
and say caption those videos?

00:02:36.359 --> 00:02:37.018
It's absurd.

00:02:37.018 --> 00:02:38.337
It is absurd.

00:02:38.417 --> 00:02:40.056
But what government does

00:02:40.060 --> 00:02:41.820
is often absurd.

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:43.580
Thank goodness for the internet

00:02:43.580 --> 00:02:45.420
and people like Kaufman,

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:47.590
someone willing to spend his own money

00:02:47.590 --> 00:02:48.329
to keep

00:02:48.329 --> 00:02:50.068
information free.

